{"parse":{"title":"Opinion polling for the 2026 Israeli legislative election","pageid":71192680,"wikitext":"{{Short description|None}}\n{{For|polling on leadership specifically|Leadership opinion polling for the 2026 Israeli legislative election}}\n{{protection padlock|small=yes}}\n{{Use dmy dates|date=September 2026}} \n\nIn the run up to the [[2026 Israeli legislative election]], various organisations are conducting [[opinion poll]]ing to gauge voting intention in [[Israel]] during the term of the [[List of members of the twenty-fifth Knesset|twenty-fifth Knesset]]. This article lists the results of such polls. The date range for these opinion polls is from the [[2022 Israeli legislative election]], held on 1 November, to the present day. In keeping with the [[election silence]] law, no polls may be published from the end of the Friday before the election until the [[polling station]]s close on election day at 22:00.<ref name=\"silence\">[[s:he:חוק הבחירות (דרכי תעמולה)#סעיף 16ה]] (ח) (in Hebrew)</ref>\n\nPolls are listed in reverse chronological order and using the dates when the survey fieldwork was done, as opposed to the date of publication. Where the fieldwork dates are unknown, the date of publication is given instead. The highest figure in each polling survey is displayed in bold with its background shaded in the leading party's colour. If a tie occurs, this is applied to the highest figures.\n\n{{TOC limit}}\n\n== Pollsters and publishers ==\nThe below table only lists pollsters and publishers that regularly publish mandate polls. \n{| class=\"wikitable\"\n|+\n!Publisher\n!Polling firm\n!Period of use\n|-\n| rowspan=\"3\" |[[Channel 13 (Israel)|Channel 13]]\n| style=\"background:#FFCCFF\" |Camil Fuchs, Midgam Project, Stat-Net<ref>{{Cite news |author1=[[Hila Korach]]|author2=[[Raviv Drucker]] |title=סקר חדשות 13: גוש נתניהו יורד ל-58 מנדטים, מרצ עוברת |url=https://13tv.co.il/item/news/politics/politics/new-survey-903379652/ |access-date=2 January 2023 |dat